      "role": "user",
      "content": "100-32=68."
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "reasoning": "Die diskriminant is korrek. Vervang nou die waardes in die kwadratiese formule en bereken albei wortels. [TOOL CHECK: calculator(expression=\"10**2 - 4*1*8\") -> 68] [TOOL CHECK: calculator(expression=\"sqrt(68)\") -> 8.246211251235321] [TOOL CHECK: calculator(expression=\"(-10 + sqrt(68))/2\") -> -0.8768943743823394] [TOOL CHECK: calculator(expression=\"(-10 - sqrt(68))/2\") -> -9.123105625617661]. Afgerond tot twee desimale plekke is die wortels -0,88 en -9,12.",
      "content": "Mooi, die diskriminant is $68$. Gebruik nou die formule:\n\n$x=\\frac{-10\\pm\\sqrt{68}}{2}$\n\nDit gee $x\\approx-0,88$ of $x\\approx-9,12$ (tot twee desimale plekke)."
    }
  ],
  "meta": {
    "strategy_used": "step_walkthrough",
    "final_answer": "$x = -0,88 \\text{ of } x = -9,12$",
    "verify_code": "import sympy as sp\nx = sp.symbols(\"x\")\nroots = sp.solve(x**2 + 10*x + 8, x)\nvals = sorted((float(sp.N(r)) for r in roots), reverse=True)\nformatted = [f\"{v:.2f}\".replace(\".\", \",\") for v in vals]\nprint(f\"x = {formatted[0]} of {formatted[1]}\")",
    "techniques": [
